      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Object Storage Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS S3 for the object storage implementation. It seems like the most straightforward option with ample documentation, which will be helpful. I'll be focused on writing a Python script to create the presigned download URL with the AWS SDK.\n\n\n**Implementing Presigned URLs**\n\nI am now writing `presigned_download.py` which will generate signed download URLs. I've decided to proceed with AWS S3, utilizing the `boto3` library, with a clear function definition that takes the bucket name, object name, and expiration time as input. The script will use `boto3` to create the presigned URL, thus, I will specify AWS S3 as the provider in the code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789821044811,
          "start": 1789821042631
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a5bfc7001YUM7qRys2ZoIg7",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a5ba570016Tq4SBMiinlWs1",
      "session_id": "ses_f465a45b7ffetPrUVjmdLCRIZH",
      "time_created": 1789821042631,
      "time_updated": 1789821044812
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "zE3JTtTXavON4siB",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import NoCredentialsError\n\ndef create_presigned_download_url(bucket_name: str, object_name: str, expiration: int = 3600):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a time-limited presigned URL for downloading a stored object from AWS S3.\n\n    Args:\n        bucket_name (str): The name of the S3 bucket.\n        object_name (str): The name of the object in the S3 bucket.\n        expiration (int): The number of seconds the presigned URL is valid for (default: 3600 seconds).\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The presigned URL if successful, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client(\n        's3',\n        aws_access_key_id=os.environ.get(\"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\"),\n        aws_secret_access_key=os.environ.get(\"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\"),\n        aws_session_token=os.environ.get(\"AWS_SESSION_TOKEN\")\n    )\n    try:\n        response = s3_client.generate_presigned_url(\n            'get_object',\n            Params={'Bucket': bucket_name, 'Key': object_name},\n            ExpiresIn=expiration\n        )\n    except NoCredentialsError:\n        print(\"AWS credentials not found. Please set AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY environment variables.\")\n        return None\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error generating presigned URL: {e}\")\n        return None\n    return response\n",
            "filePath": "presigned_download.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
